WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:04.899
If you plan on going into the fourth Avengers
movie totally spoiler-free, then we wish you

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:05.800
the best of luck.

00:00:06.049 --> 00:00:09.960
But if you just can't wait until the movie
comes out to try and figure out what happens,

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:13.100
we've got some of the most compelling rumors
rounded up right here.

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:17.880
It's been awhile since we've seen Captain
America in charge of a full-fledged team of

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:18.440
Avengers.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:23.100
Since the events of Civil War, he's been running
around in the shadows, doing his work as a

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:25.200
fugitive with a small, loyal group.

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:29.620
But Thanos appears to be the just what the
Marvel Cinematic Universe needs to let bygones

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:32.660
be bygones, and get the band back together
in a big way.

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:37.500
A purportedly leaked image from the marketing
materials for the fourth Avengers film seems

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:42.240
to reveal Cap leading a new team of Avengers
in an ultimate battle against the Mad Titan.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:47.370
If it's real, then the revamped team will
consist of Iron Man, Black Widow, Hulk, Hawkeye

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:50.720
and Thor, along with War Machine and Scott
Lang's Ant-Man.

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:56.540
Also present is newcomer Captain Marvel, Guardians
of the Galaxy member Rocket, and Nebula, daughter

00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:57.320
of Thanos.

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:02.220
The image also reveals Cap to have cleaned
up since his grungier days in Infinity War,

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:04.540
clean-shaven and back in a star-spangled suit.

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:09.040
It doesn't show his classic shield, but with
a lineup like this, does he really even need

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:09.540
it?

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:15.040
Those familiar with Marvel comics have probably
been anticipating the arrival of the alien

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.420
Skrulls in the MCU for some time now.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:23.100
According to an Avengers 4 rumor started by
Jeremy Conrad at MCU Cosmic, Nick Fury has

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:27.600
also been waiting for the humanoid shapeshifters
to show up, which is exactly what he thought

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:30.520
was happening during the Infinity War post-credit
tag.

00:01:30.729 --> 00:01:35.820
As Conrad tells it, when people started vanishing
after Thanos snapped his fingers, Fury assumed

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:38.900
the Skrulls were to blame and called on Carol
Danvers for help.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:44.100
Conrad also claims that Hawkeye will be involved
in the Skrull storyline, hunting down Yakuza

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:47.130
in Tokyo who are secretly Skrulls in disguise.

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:50.560
It sounds like a pretty great way for him
to make his comeback after sitting things

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:51.840
out at the family farm.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:53.900
"Clearly retirement doesn't suit you.

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:55.130
Got tired of shootin' golf?"

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:57.480
"Well I played 18, shot 18.

00:01:59.080 --> 00:01:59.940
Just can't seem to miss."

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:04.940
Rumors that Avengers 4's plot will heavily
involve time travel have been out in the wild

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:09.779
ever since leaked photos first emerged of
the movie recreating scenes from the first

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:10.400
Avengers.

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:14.340
It's a pretty compelling rumor, and Ant-Man
and the Wasp might tell us everything we need

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:16.640
to know about how it's going to go down.

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:21.120
While the small-scale sequel mostly did its
own thing, the mid-credit scene dropped a

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:24.660
huge clue about how the Avengers may win the
Infinity War.

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:29.560
In the scene, Scott Lang returns to the Quantum
Realm, being advised by the first Wasp not

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:32.320
to get stuck in a "time vortex" while he's
in there.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:37.300
As the credits scene reveals, Thanos' fateful
snap takes place while Scott is still inside

00:02:37.309 --> 00:02:41.860
the Quantum Realm, leaving him stuck inside
the tiny world with no one alive to get him

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:42.360
out.

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:47.340
To escape his apparent doom, it seems plausible
that Ant-Man will risk exiting the dimension

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:49.260
through one of those time vortexes.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:50.440
Where will he end up?

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:54.900
Based on the fact that a significantly older
actress has been cast in the role of Scott's

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:59.120
daughter Cassie, it sounds like he's probably
going to the future at one point.

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:04.100
Practically since the release of Infinity
War, there's been a theory that the seemingly-dead

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:09.020
Avengers are actually trapped in a pocket
world inside of the mysterious Soul Stone.

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:11.360
There's plenty of precedent for the theory.

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:16.060
In Marvel Comics, the Soul Gem houses the
Soulworld, a pocket dimension that acts as

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:17.260
a kind of purgatory.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:19.420
And we may have already seen the place.

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:23.269
Some believe that the orange-colored, dream-like
scene in which Thanos talks to young Gamora

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:28.430
after her death in Infinity War may take place
inside the stone, with her death having been

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:31.260
crucial to Thanos getting the stone in the
first place.

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:35.400
But if this is all true, how will the living
Avengers get into the Soul World, and how

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:36.880
will the snapped ones get out?

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:38.340
That, we do not know.

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:44.099
Speaking on a panel at the 2018 Austin Film
Festival, Marvel Studios producer Michael

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:49.620
Grillo revealed that one Doctor Strange actor
is unexpectedly returning to the MCU.

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:53.989
Speaking about the difficulty in scheduling
actors for the massive production, Grillo

00:03:53.989 --> 00:03:58.249
seemed to let it slip that the Ancient One
would be returning for Avengers 4 in some

00:03:58.249 --> 00:03:58.980
capacity.

00:03:59.249 --> 00:04:01.819
Discussing time constraints, Grillo reportedly
said,

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:05.540
"When we got Tilda Swinton, she was just a
one-day availability."

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:09.629
If you don't remember, the Ancient One appeared
to be fatally wounded during the events of

00:04:09.629 --> 00:04:14.160
Doctor Strange, passing on after one last
pep talk to the Sorcerer Supreme.

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:18.460
Considering her decisive-looking death and
her established knowledge of time travel,

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:21.320
she's probably coming back as part of a time
travel plot.

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:25.580
As a former guardian of the Time Stone who
was alive for thousands of years, she could

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:30.200
have vital intel for the surviving Avengers,
even if she doesn't go head-to-head with Thanos

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:30.700
herself.

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:35.919
One of the biggest surprises in Avengers:
Infinity War was the return of Red Skull,

00:04:35.919 --> 00:04:39.770
and it appears as though its upcoming sequel
will bring another Captain America villain

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:40.880
back with a bang.

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:46.919
Speaking to the UFC Unfiltered podcast in
October 2018, Crossbones actor Frank Grillo

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:51.039
revealed that the deadly assassin and HYDRA
agent was going to be making an appearance

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:52.220
in Avengers 4.

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:52.880
But how?

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:57.260
After all, Crossbones died when he tried to
blow himself up on Steve Rogers, right?

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:59.480
Throwing caution to the wind, Grillo said,

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:02.780
"He makes an appearance in the next Avengers
movie, but it's a flashback.

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:06.699
[...] I'm allowed to say whatever I want because
I'm never doing another Marvel movie.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:08.540
[…] I'm 117 years old."

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:12.460
Grillo later tried to walk back his comments,
but the damage was already done.

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:16.430
It all adds up to a pretty clear suggestion
about where this next chapter in the Infinity

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:17.760
War story is going.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:22.740
But if time travel really is where the story
is going, why Earth's Mightiest Heroes need

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:25.419
to revisit this particular villain remains
to be seen.

